better to discard F4. \n\nSo the answer is Play F4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand has potential for forming chows in B7-B8-B9 and possibly pungs in W3. Discarding F4 (seat wind) is safer than F2 (prevailing wind) to preserve potential for Seat Wind points. Keeping B7-B8-B9 intact supports forming a chow, which is essential for scoring patterns like All Chows or Mixed Straight.\n\nReason: Discarding F4 (North Wind) avoids losing potential Seat Wind points and preserves key tiles for chow formation. F2 (South Wind, prevailing wind) should be retained for possible Prevalent Wind scoring. B7-B8-B9 form a critical chow in the Dots suit, which supports multiple scoring patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play F4"}
